<title>JAPAN: Japan August tin imports off 12.4 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan August tin imports off 12.4 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan imported 2,250 tonnes of refined tin in August, off 12.4 percent from 2,568 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The imports were as follows (on a customs-cleared basis in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    August 96	 July 96	August 95</p>
<p> Total		2,250	    1,819	    2,568</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Indonesia	  1,157		878		836</p>
<p> Malaysia	     521		479		780</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first eight months of 1996 were 17,043 tonnes, versus 59,752 tonnes in the same period last year. --Tokyo Commodities Desk (813 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
